{"session_id":"b606e9ca-b863-4906-850e-562afca2707c","transcript_path":"/home/youran/.claude/projects/-mnt-d-research-YouranSun-github-io/b606e9ca-b863-4906-850e-562afca2707c.jsonl","cwd":"/mnt/d/research/YouranSun.github.io","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/home/youran/.claude/projects/-mnt-d-research-YouranSun-github-io/memory/user_profile.md","content":"---\nname: user-profile\ndescription: Youran Sun's background, research interests, and competitive programming achievements\nmetadata:\n  type: user\n---\n\nYouran Sun (孙悠然) is a junior undergraduate at CUHK-Shenzhen (graduating 2027), double majoring in Computer Science & Engineering and Interdisciplinary Data Analytics. Email: youransun@berkeley.edu (Berkeley visit) / youransun@link.cuhk.edu.cn.\n\n**Research interests:** Data agents, LLM-powered data processing (semantic data processing), RAG systems, graph data management.\n\n**Research experience:**\n- 2026.5–now: Research intern at Tsinghua University DB Group, supervised by Prof. Guoliang Li and Prof. Ji Sun\n- 2026.1–2026.5: Visiting UC Berkeley, supervised by Prof. Aditya Parameswaran, collaborating with Dr. Sepanta Zeighami (EPIC Data Lab)\n- 2024.1–2025.12: CUHK-SZ, supervised by Prof. Yixiang Fang and Dr. Yingli Zhou\n\n**Publications:**\n- HOLDUP (under revision at VLDB 2027): semantic data processing with holistic data understanding; co-first author with Zeighami, Parameswaran group\n- DynamicICS (SIGMOD 2026): efficient influential community search over dynamic graphs; first author\n- AnchoredDS (SIGMOD 2026): efficient anchored densest subgraph discovery; 2nd author\n- GraphRAG (VLDB 2025): in-depth analysis of graph-based RAG; 3rd author, 1.5K GitHub stars\n- PITAI: currently commented out/hidden (under review or withdrawn)\n\n**Competitive programming:**\n- ICPC/CCPC gold medalist multiple times; NOI bronze + girls' 1st prize\n- Student leader of CUHK-SZ CP team (Jun 2024 – Dec 2025), ~30 members\n- Actively works on gender inclusion and knowledge access in competitive programming\n\n**Seeking:** PhD position for Fall 2027.\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CPkhZK3m4ZUGEWLWVhaume","logged_at":"2026-06-17T23:12:03"}
